<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela delays Orinoco oil decision again.</title>
<headline>Venezuela delays Orinoco oil decision again.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela's Congress delayed for a third time a meeting expected to approve the $3.5 billion Hamaca oil project in the Orinoco Tar Belt, congressional sources said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>They said Wednesday's bicamaral Energy and Mines Committee was suspended after congressmen were held up in a meeting to elect a new president of the Senate, and a new date for the Committee meeting had not been decided.</p>
<p>The Committee is expected to approve the Hamaca project involving Venezuela's state oil subsidiary Corpoven, ARCO, Texaco and Phillips.</p>
<p>((--Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
</text>
